{"id":"v7","level":4,"levelName":"The verb system","n":12,"of":15,"title":"Telling someone to do it","titleHe":"צִוּוּי","goal":"Give an order — the textbook way and the way people actually speak.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"There is a proper imperative, and it's what you'll read in books and signs."},{"type":"table","caption":"Imperatives","head":["binyan","to a man","to a woman","to a group"],"rows":[["פָּעַל — write","כְּתֹב","כִּתְבִי","כִּתְבוּ"],["פִּעֵל — speak","דַּבֵּר","דַּבְּרִי","דַּבְּרוּ"],["הִפְעִיל — explain","הַסְבֵּר","הַסְבִּירִי","הַסְבִּירוּ"]]},{"type":"text","body":"In speech, Israelis mostly use the future tense instead, which sounds softer: תִּכְתֹּב rather than כְּתֹב."},{"type":"tip","body":"The negative imperative has no choice — it is always אַל plus the future. אַל תֵּלֵךְ, don't go. לֹא תֵּלֵךְ is not a command; it means you will not go."}],"vocab":[{"he":"בּוֹא","en":"come! (m.)","translit":"bo"},{"he":"בּוֹאִי","en":"come! (f.)","translit":"bo'i"},{"he":"תֵּן","en":"give! (m.)","translit":"ten"},{"he":"סְלִיחָה","en":"excuse me, sorry","translit":"slicha"},{"he":"אַל","en":"don't (with the future)","translit":"al"},{"he":"חַכֵּה","en":"wait! (m.)","translit":"chake"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["as long as","similar","Passover","come! (m.)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בּוֹא","translit":"bo"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["interesting","come! (f.)","Tishrei (Sept–Oct)","this (after the noun, m.)"],"correct":1,"prompt":"בּוֹאִי","translit":"bo'i"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["mourning","wakes up","narrative, legend","give! (m.)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"תֵּן","translit":"ten"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["in fact","more","excuse me, sorry","peace"],"correct":2,"prompt":"סְלִיחָה","translit":"slicha"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["near","don't (with the future)","narrative, legend","mouse"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אַל","translit":"al"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["good night","wait! (m.)","tea","an exile, one banished"],"correct":1,"prompt":"חַכֵּה","translit":"chake"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “wait! (m.)”?","options":["לְגַבֵּי","חַכֵּה","אִישׁ","אַל"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “excuse me, sorry”?","options":["מִשְׁפָּחָה","סְלִיחָה","אִם","הָעִיר"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["בּוֹא","come! (m.)"],["בּוֹאִי","come! (f.)"],["תֵּן","give! (m.)"],["סְלִיחָה","excuse me, sorry"],["אַל","don't (with the future)"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “come! (m.)”?","options":["קִדּוּשׁ","יָכוֹל","מִסְפָּר","בּוֹא"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["בּוֹאִי","אַל","חַכֵּה","בּוֹא"],"correct":2,"say":"חַכֵּה","he":true},{"type":"read","he":"אַל","translit":"al","en":"don't (with the future)"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “come! (f.)”?","options":["עֲבוֹדָה","דָּרוֹם","יַיִן","בּוֹאִי"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"“Don't go” (to a man) is —","options":["אַל תֵּלֵךְ","לֹא תֵּלֵךְ","אַל הָלַךְ","לֹא לֵךְ"],"correct":0,"why":"Negative commands use אַל with the future. לֹא תֵּלֵךְ is a prediction, not an order."},{"type":"type","q":"Write “wait! (m.)” in Hebrew","answer":"חַכֵּה","hint":"chake"}]}